## Context

The 2026-09-07 whole-repository review of `oscardvs/zoteus` found five
contained, user-visible defects suitable for ordinary public issues. A sixth
public issue should ask the maintainer to enable GitHub private vulnerability
reporting. GitHub authentication did not complete in the filing session, so
the work is retained here instead of being silently lost.

This ticket also owns the follow-through: bring substantive upstream comments,
reviews, requested changes, merges, and fixes back into this repository's
record, with the smallest response or patch plan each one requires.

## Public issue queue

1. Resolve the effective library consistently for writes and annotations.
2. Package the native PDF dependency for every platform advertised by the
   MCPB, or narrow the advertised platform support to what is verified.
3. Do not advance the library cursor when incremental own-words/note catch-up
   fails.
4. Support bibliography generation from a key-free local Zotero library.
5. Keep note passages from crowding distinct items out of semantic-search
   results.
6. Enable GitHub private vulnerability reporting. This issue is deliberately
   neutral and contains no vulnerability details.

## Filing rules

- Re-check each public finding against live upstream `main` immediately before
  filing; do not file work already fixed or duplicated by an existing issue.
- One coherent defect per issue. Include a minimal reproduction, expected and
  actual behaviour, the smallest plausible fix shape, and acceptance criteria.
- Keep internal governance and all security-sensitive evidence out of public
  issue text.
- Ask only for the confidential reporting channel in issue 6. If it becomes
  available, use it for security-sensitive reports rather than a public issue.
- Record every filed URL and every substantive response in this ticket with
  `erg log`; do not infer approval from silence.

## Exit criteria

- [x] The five functional findings are revalidated against current upstream.
- [x] Existing upstream issues are checked for duplicates.
- [x] Five public functional issues are filed, or this ticket logs why a
      finding was deliberately not filed.
- [x] The neutral private-vulnerability-reporting request is filed without
      security details.
- [x] Each filed issue URL is recorded here.
- [ ] Substantive maintainer feedback is relayed here with the smallest
      appropriate response or patch plan.

## References

- `GOVERNANCE.md`, especially the disclosure rule and courtesy-filing norm.
- `SYNC.md` for live upstream state and the reviewed baseline.
- GitHub documentation: `https://docs.github.com/code-security/security-advisories/working-with-repository-security-advisories/configuring-private-vulnerability-reporting-for-a-repository`.

## Evidence and handoff

- `verification/UPSTREAM-PUBLIC-REVIEW-0736.md` records revalidation,
  duplicate review, probe commands, limitations and the raw-evidence paths.
- `verification/upstream-issues-0736/` holds the exact filed public bodies
  and verified creation receipts.
- Filing is complete. Follow-through stays open: read the filed pages and
  associated fixes, record substantive responses with `erg log`, and name the
  smallest response or patch plan. No background monitoring is configured.
